er</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Feldmeier</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Epidemiology and morbidity of scabies and pediculosis capitis in resource-poor communities in Brazil</article-title><source>Br J Dermatol</source><volume>153</volume><fpage>150</fpage><lpage>156</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16029341</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040295-b031"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group><name><surname>Mehta</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><source>Maximum city: Bombay lost and found</source><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Alfred A</publisher-name> Knopf.				</citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040295-b032"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Dziuban</surname><given-names>EJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Liang</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></name><name><surname>Craun</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name><name><surname>Hill</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Yu</surname><given-names>PA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Surveillance for waterborne disease and outbreaks associated with recreational water&#x02014;United States, 2003&#x02013;2004</article-title><source>MMWR Surveill Summ</source><volume>55</volume><fpage>1</fpage><lpage>30</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17183230</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pmed-0040295-b033"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group><name><surname>Ko</surname><given-names>AI</given-names></name><name><surname>Galvao Reis</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ribeiro Dourado</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>WD</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Riley</surname><given-names>LW</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Urban epidem